095 - Spring Has Now Unwrapped the Flowers
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 95
Topic: God the Father - 

Verse 1:
[Em/B]Spring has now [Am]unwrapped [G]the [D/F#]flowers, [C/G]Day [G]is [C/G]fast [D/A]reviving,
[G/B]Life in [C]all [D7/C]her [G]growing [Bm/F#]powers [Em/B]Towards [G]the [Am]light [G]is [C/G]striving:
[Bm]Gone [F#dim]the [G]iron touch [C/G]of [D/A]cold, [G]Winter [Em]time [D/F#]and [G]frost [Em/B]time,
[G]Seedlings, working through the [C/G]mould, [Bm/F#]Now [F#dim]make up [G]for [C]lost [Em/B]time.

Verse 2:
[Em/B]Herb and plant [D/F#]that [C/G]winter [Em/B]long,
[Em/B]Slumbered at [D/F#]their [C/G]leisurek,
[G/B]Now [C]be [G]stirring, [Em/B]green [Am]and [C/G]strong,
[G/B]Find [D7/C]in [D/F#]growth [G]their pleasure:
[Bm]All [G]the world [D/A]with [Em]beauty fills,
[Bm]Gold [G]the green enhacing;
[G]Flowers [F#dim]make [G]glee [Bm/F#]among [G]the [C]hills,
